  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="3f4d-cac4-a967-da42" name="Gallic (Hannibal) - List Notes" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false">
      <description>GALLIC ARMY LIST (Hannibal &amp; the Punic Wars, pp.80-81)
Represents the Celtic tribes of northern Italy and the Mediterranean coast; may also represent northern Spanish tribes. Characters up to 25%; at least one must be the overall leader; if no High Chieftain is taken the commander must be a Chieftain. Infantry at least 50%; Cavalry and Chariots up to 25%; Supporting Infantry up to 20%.
Allies: limited documentation; Hannibal's Boii and Insubres are better represented as Gallic allies for a Carthaginian army.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Gallic]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Cavalry and Chariots: up to 25%
  Supporting Infantry: up to 20%
  Standard Gallic composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
